# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sidebase environment variables
#
# The frontend needs NO environment variables — nothing secret ever ships to the
# browser. Everything below is used only by the Cloudflare Worker (worker/ +
# functions/) and must be set as secrets: `npx wrangler secret put NAME`, or in
#   Cloudflare dashboard → Workers & Pages → sidebase → Settings → Variables and Secrets
#
# For local development copy this file to `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) and fill it in.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Stripe secret key. Use sk_test_… while testing, sk_live_… in production.
# Store as an ENCRYPTED secret in Cloudflare.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me

# Signing secret of your Stripe webhook endpoint (whsec_…).
# Locally, `stripe listen` prints one. Store as an ENCRYPTED secret in Cloudflare.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me

# Optional: a Stripe Price ID (price_…) for the $7.99 report. If unset, Checkout
# uses an inline $7.99 USD price, so you can sell without creating a product first.
# Test-mode and live-mode Price IDs are different — set the matching one.
STRIPE_PRICE_ID=

# Optional canonical public URL (Stripe redirects, sitemap.xml, robots.txt). Leave unset
# to use whatever address the site is served on (e.g. your *.workers.dev URL). Set it to
# https://sidebase.cc once that domain is attached to the Worker.
# SITE_URL=https://sidebase.cc

# Binding (not a variable): a Workers KV namespace bound as PURCHASES.
# Already declared in wrangler.jsonc. Locally, `npm run dev:full` creates one automatically.
